  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nAnother cold front will move east through the area on Sunday \nwhich may bring a brief window for rain chances Sunday evening \nand overnight, mainly across far Northeast Ohio and Northwest \nPennsylvania. Total rainfall amounts are expected to be light \nand less than a tenth of an inch. Behind this front, an area of \nCanadian high pressure will build south into the region, \nushering in cooler and drier air. Will continue to watch \ntemperature trends for frost potential Monday night into Tuesday\nwith high pressure directly overhead, though guidance has \nleveled off somewhat in terms of low temperature magnitude \n(upper 30s), which could limit the overall frost threat. \nMeanwhile, the frost potential appears to be decreasing for \nTuesday night into Wednesday morning as guidance is favoring a \nfaster onset of warm air advection from the west. \n\nAnother weak cold front may cross the area by the end of the week, \nthough the latest guidance suggests a mainly dry frontal \npassage with ample mid-level dry air in place.",
